# WN22-SO-000130: Windows Server 2022 required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000130-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon.`
    description `Failure to display the logon banner prior to a logon attempt will negate legal proceedings resulting from unauthorized access to system resources. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006, SRG-OS-000024-GPOS-00007, SRG-OS-000228-GPOS-00088`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,reg-sz,medium`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-53:AC-8`
    control_objective `WN22-SO-000130`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Interactive Logon: Message text for users attempting to log on to the following: You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only. By using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions: -The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on thi`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_AC_8 `Windows Server implements AC-8 by setting registry value 'LegalNoticeText' (REG_SZ) under 'HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System' to the STIG-required value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match. Remediation sets the value via Group Policy or direct registry edit.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System`
        name `LegalNoticeText`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value string contains `U.S. Government (USG) Information System`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
